\nSeminars & Events\nShow submenu for Seminars & Events\nUpcoming Seminars\nDurham Symposia\nCollingwood Lecture Series\nPascal Lecture Series\nDistinguished Lecture Series\nInternational Women's Day Talks\nBlack History Month Lectures\nResearch & Impact\nShow submenu for Research & Impact\nResearch Areas\nImpact\nFellowships\nEDI & Outreach\nShow submenu for EDI & Outreach\nEquality, Diversity & Inclusion\nOutreach\nResources\nWomen in Maths\nFirst-Generation Scholars\nDecolonisation\nPublic Engagement\nSchool Outreach\nWidening Participation\nCurrent Students & Staff\nShow submenu for Current Students & Staff\nUG Maths Students Area\nPGT Maths Students Area\nPGR Maths Students Area\nMaths Staff Area\nREF 2021 Result\nShow submenu for REF 2021 Result\nPostgraduate Study\nThe Department of Mathematical Sciences is one of the leading research units in the country, with interests in a wide range of areas in pure mathematics, applied mathematics, mathematical and theoretical physics, as well as statistics and probability. One measure of the vibrancy of our research is the number of postgraduate students we attract. There are about fifty at any given time within the Department.\nOn completion of their course, taught postgraduates may progress to further study (in Durham or elsewhere) towards a related PhD, or undertake a teaching qualification. Others enter careers such as medical physics. Research postgraduates have similarly varied career paths; example job titles include operational researcher, actuarial analyst and postgraduate researcher. Example employers include the Civil Service, Deloitte, the Ministry of Defence, and Universities.\nDurham is University of the Year 2026\nWe are The Times and The Sunday Times Good University Guide University of the Year 2026. We are also joint runner-up University of the Year for Graduate Employment and ranked third overall, up two places from last year.\nDiscover our Postgraduate Programmes\nFind out more about our Postgraduate Taught and Research Degrees.\nTaught Degrees\nFind out more about our Postgraduate Taught Degrees.\nResearch Degrees\nFind out more about our Postgraduate Research Degrees.\nI enjoyed the choice of modules and I was given practical skills which have helped me in my professional life. For me, the dissertation was the most enjoyable part of the course. The chance to explore a subject in depth on my own was very rewarding.\nOwen Bell\nMathematics and MISCADA graduate, Durham University\nInformation for New PGT Students\nFind out more about what to keep in mind before you arrive at Durham University and once term begins.\nInformation for New PGT Students\nLook closer at our Department of Mathematical Sciences\nOur Department of Mathematical Sciences combines world-leading research with a dedication to the learning experience of our students. We offer a unique blend of high-quality teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines and provide practical experience to support future careers and employment prospects.\nMore about the Department of Mathematical Sciences\nWhat is your favourite thing about Durham?\nMeet Peter Liu from China, studying MMath Mathematics, and discover what his favourite thing is about studying maths at Durham University.\nLearn more about the MMath in Mathematics\nDepartment of Mathematical Sciences on LinkedIn\nGet updates and stay in touch - follow us on LinkedIn. Our graduate community is diverse and international, and goes on to explore destinations around the world, with many taking on senior leadership roles in their companies and institutions.\nVisit and follow our LinkedIn page\nDiscover more\nScholarships\nFind out more about available Scholarships.\nResearch and Impact\nFind out more about our research.\nScholarships\nFind out more about available Scholarships.\nResearch and Impact\nFind out more about our research.\nEmployability\nLearn more about employability and career destinations of our postgraduate students.\nInternational